<title>HONG KONG: China Eastern has five A340s, nine MD-90s on order.</title>
<headline>China Eastern has five A340s, nine MD-90s on order.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>China Eastern Airlines Corp Ltd said in its prospectus released on Monday that it had five Airbus Industrie and nine McDonnell Douglas Corp aircraft on order.</p>
<p>&quot;The company added three new Airbus A340 aircraft in 1996 to its fleet and has entered into contracts to acquire five additional A340 aircraft and nine Mcdonnell Douglas MD-90 aircraft to be delivered between 1997 and 2000,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>The prospectus did not state when the orders were made.</p>
<p>An order for three A340s had been confirmed in April 1996, while an order for nine MD-90s was signed in July 1996.</p>
</text>
